[quote="Envisioner"]

 I&#39;m not counting him any more than I&#39;m counting the Vengeance Five, nor do I consider Scholar&#39;s need for a nemesis satisfied by the Hermetic.&nbsp; I will be disappointed if the game ends without every hero having exactly one &quot;proper&quot; Nemesis.&nbsp; Even then, I&#39;ll be a little sad that the Freedom Five are as over-represented as they are (and Tempest and Unity a little bit so), because the other characters are cool too.&nbsp; But I&#39;m reconciled to the fact that the creators have chosen to focus on those five.&nbsp; I just hope they don&#39;t distort the game too much more than that overall.&nbsp; A person whose favorite hero is Visionary or Omnitron-X shouldn&#39;t feel like they&#39;re missing out on some of the game&#39;s awesomeness because they get so many fewer nemesis &quot;pings&quot; than someone who favored Wraith or Tachyon would. 

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Consider the Mini nemeses give one to every hero already released, I don&#39;t think these are going to be the &#39;Only&#39; nemesis at all for those heroes who have not yet had a &#39;main&#39; nemesis.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

From the looks of it, everyone will have 2 nemesis - their &#39;Main&#39; and a small one, and then the Freedom Five have the Vengeance Five and the Freedom Six have Iron Legacy to boot. I would not be surprised to see more &#39;Mini Nemesis&#39; for farther released heroes down the line.
